# Rank 1287 / CVE-2026-32763: kysely's MySQL JSON path literal for
# eb.ref(col, '->$').key(key) is built by DefaultQueryCompiler
# (src/query-compiler/default-query-compiler.ts). visitJSONPathLeg opens a
# fragment with `this.append("'$")`, then splices the leg's value straight
# into the SQL text with `this.append(String(node.value))`, and closes with
# `this.append("'")` -- a raw string coercion sitting unescaped between two
# single quotes, so a key containing `'` closes the literal early and the
# rest of the key parses as SQL (CWE-89). Fix 0a602bff2f routes the string
# case through the compiler's own sanitizeStringLiteral (doubles embedded
# `'`), leaving the non-string branch as String(node.value) since array
# indexes and 'last'/'#-N' never carry a quote. The project's own
# regression test injects `first' as X from Y; drop table person -- `
# through exactly this call (GHSA-wmrf-hv6w-mr66: >= 0.26.0, <= 0.28.11,
# patched 0.28.12).
#
# The vulnerable splice is present at 0.26.0 (default-query-compiler.ts:1361
# at that tag), 0.27.0, 0.27.6, 0.28.5 and 0.28.11, and the compiler has no
# JSON path handling at all at 0.25.0 or 0.25.5 -- the advisory's lower
# bound is the construct's first release. `git tag --contains 0a602bff2f`
# names v0.28.12 first, matching the advisory's patched version.
#
# The weakness is inside the library's compiler, and the caller's
# eb.ref(col, '->$').key(key) is correct code on both sides of the fix, so
# the report that belongs to this CVE is the dependency finding: an npm pin
# of kysely below 0.28.12, the first release carrying the sanitized leg.
# The feed holds one threshold per artifact, so pins below the advisory's
# 0.26.0 lower bound report too; those releases do not contain the
# construct (verified at 0.25.5) and that over-match is this row's stated
# residual. Non-registry specifiers share it: `file:`/`link:`/`workspace:`
# pins carry no comparable version and read as below the floor, which is
# how the library's own tree (test/bun's link:kysely,
# test/outdated-ts's file:../../) reports while its example app's 0.23.3
# pin and test/composite-ts's ^0.28.9 pin report as genuine below-floor
# versions.
#
# The code-level shape stays unreachable and the ENGINE-GAPS "1287" entry
# stays open: `append` mutates the private field `#sql`, set inside
# `append` (called from `visitJSONPathLeg`) and read back inside
# `compileQuery`/`getSql()` -- several methods on one receiver joined only
# by `this`, no argument or return value carrying the leg's value across
# the last hop. `vyql trace` still dead-ends identically on both revisions
# at the `this.#sql += str` statement (`call=this.#sql`, no outgoing flow,
# callee not traced), the TypeScript private-field instance of the
# aliasReceiverSelf field-crossing family recorded for 1198 (PHP) and 1740
# (Ruby). The four code-form tests below hold that gap open on both sides
# of the fix. A trap while isolating it: lowering.go's mutatorMethods
# treats a fixed name vocabulary (append, write, add, push, set, ...) as
# taint-transferring by call-site method name alone, so the isolating pair
# avoids every name on that list on the write side (addPart, build);
# `append` stays in the primary repro because that is kysely's actual
# method name, and it is the innermost hop either way.

test "rank1287: a kysely pin below the first sanitized JSON-path release is a dependency finding"
  lang javascript
  file src/handler.ts
  code
  ```
  import { Kysely, sql } from 'kysely'

  interface Database {
    people: { data: string }
  }

  export async function firstNames(
    db: Kysely<Database>,
    req: { query: { key: string } },
  ) {
    const key = req.query.key
    return db
      .with('people', (eb) =>
        eb
          .selectFrom('person')
          .select(sql<{ data: string }>`json_object('first', first_name)`.as('data')),
      )
      .selectFrom('people')
      .select((eb) => eb.ref('data', '->$').key(key).as('first'))
      .execute()
  }
  ```
  file package.json
  code
  ```
  {
    "name": "app",
    "dependencies": {
      "kysely": "0.28.11"
    }
  }
  ```
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 CVE-2026-32763
  expect VYQL-SCA-002

